  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The maximum particle velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p>And the wave velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>For wave velocity to be equal to maximum particle&nbsp;velocity</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
